              "id": 18098296,
              "is_private": false,
              "raw_text": "**Environment:**\nOperating system: Linux\nFirefox version: Firefox 150.0\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\nWhat happened:\n\n    When using Google Meet on Firefox (Linux), I experience severe performance degradation. Audio and video are extremely choppy, and I frequently receive \"Your connection is lost\" notifications. Screen sharing often causes the entire session to become unusable or drop entirely.\n\nExpected behavior:\n\n    The meeting should run smoothly without artificial bandwidth throttling, similar to the experience on Chromium-based browsers.\n\nAdditional Context:\n\n        This is NOT a network issue. On the same machine, network, and at the same time, Chromium-based browsers work perfectly with no lag or interruptions, even during screen sharing.\n\n        System: Debian Sid, KDE Plasma 6.\n\n        Hardware: AMD Ryzen 7 5700U (Dell Vostro 3525).\n\n        It seems to be a WebRTC congestion control or hardware acceleration handling issue specific to the Gecko engine when interacting with Meet.\n\n**Actual Behavior:**\nPerformance issues with a limited bandwith\n\n**Notes:**\n- The issue is believed to be valid, but was not reproduced\n\nCreated from https://github.com/webcompat/web-bugs/issues/220995",
              "reactions": {},
              "tags": [],
              "text": "**Environment:**\nOperating system: Linux\nFirefox version: Firefox 150.0\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\nWhat happened:\n\n    When using Google Meet on Firefox (Linux), I experience severe performance degradation. Audio and video are extremely choppy, and I frequently receive \"Your connection is lost\" notifications. Screen sharing often causes the entire session to become unusable or drop entirely.\n\nExpected behavior:\n\n    The meeting should run smoothly without artificial bandwidth throttling, similar to the experience on Chromium-based browsers.\n\nAdditional Context:\n\n        This is NOT a network issue. On the same machine, network, and at the same time, Chromium-based browsers work perfectly with no lag or interruptions, even during screen sharing.\n\n        System: Debian Sid, KDE Plasma 6.\n\n        Hardware: AMD Ryzen 7 5700U (Dell Vostro 3525).\n\n        It seems to be a WebRTC congestion control or hardware acceleration handling issue specific to the Gecko engine when interacting with Meet.\n\n**Actual Behavior:**\nPerformance issues with a limited bandwith\n\n**Notes:**\n- The issue is believed to be valid, but was not reproduced\n\nCreated from https://github.com/webcompat/web-bugs/issues/220995",
              "time": "2026-05-22T11:04:37Z"
